body:
In [Source/Templates/gcc/linker/STM32H563xx_RAM.ld](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/cmsis_device_h5/blob/v1.1.0/Source/Templates/gcc/linker/STM32H563xx_RAM.ld), the output section is named `.ARM`. I am not sure as I am not using these but I think, this has to be named `.ARM.exidx` according to [Exception Handling ABI for the Arm® Architecture](https://github.com/ARM-software/abi-aa/blob/2a70c42d62e9c3eb5887fa50b71257f20daca6f9/ehabi32/ehabi32.rst#sections)

```
.ARM : {
    . = ALIGN(4);
    __exidx_start = .;
    *(.ARM.exidx*)
    __exidx_end = .;
    . = ALIGN(4);
  } >RAM
```

The other output section is correctly named `.ARM.extab`.

I did not check all but it might be the case for some of the other or all linker scripts.
